# A modus mentis wounds have broken cannot be used, and says which part of the body failed.
#
# THE RULE. Every anatomy source a modus mentis draws on contributes to its max level, and a wounded
# one now contributes a NEGATIVE amount — -2 for a High-handicap wound, -1 once Medium wounds have
# driven the source below zero (MaxLevelPenalty). Enough damage drags the ceiling under the base of 1
# that every modus mentis starts from, and GetEffectiveModusMentisLevel — what was learned, capped by
# what the body can still reach — lands at 0 or below. There is nothing left to roll with.
#
# WHY `cripple` EXISTS. `wound` draws from the anatomy's catalogue at random, so landing a
# High-handicap wound on one NAMED organ is a lottery a script cannot run — and breaking a particular
# modus mentis is the precondition of every test in this area. `cripple` puts one on every source the
# named modus mentis draws on.
#
# WHAT IS ASSERTED, and why it takes all three. `inspect skills` proves the level really fell — a
# refusal alone would pass on a rule that fired for some other reason. The banner proves the player
# was TOLD, in the voice of the modus mentis that failed and naming the organs, which is the whole
# point of refusing rather than filtering. And the noetic count proves it was charged for like every
# other refusal (ActionRulesChecker's rule costs a point; only a ChoiceRules withholding is free).
#
# The clamp is derived, never stored, so `save roundtrip` must still pass with a broken modus mentis
# on the body: the stored level is what was learned and is what goes in the file.
#
# NOTE the wound reaches more than it was aimed at, and that is correct. A visage wound disables the
# eyes AND the nose, so one `cripple` breaks every modus mentis built on either. Hence `broken=True`
# rather than an assertion naming one id.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --grant-mm woodcraft:3 --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 45
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 45
advance 12 90

# Sound to begin with: woodcraft stands at the level it was granted, and nothing is broken.
inspect skills
expect-state skills "woodcraft level=3 xp=0 effective=3 max=3 broken=False"
expect-no-state skills "broken=True"

# Ruin every organ woodcraft is built on. The stored level is untouched — it is what was LEARNED —
# and only the effective level falls, which is what makes this heal when the wound does.
cripple woodcraft
inspect skills
expect-state skills "woodcraft level=3 xp=0 effective=0 max=0 broken=True"

# Choosing a broken modus mentis for an observation is offered and refused, not hidden. The refusal
# is narrated in that modus mentis's own voice and names the organs and the wounds behind them.
click keyword 0
choose 1
choose 0
advance 8 90
expect "will not answer"
expect "cannot look at anything"

# It cost a point, exactly as an action refused by a coded rule does.
state
expect "NOETIC"

# A broken modus mentis is a derived state, so nothing about it reaches the file.
save roundtrip

quit
